# 10. SAVING, PERFORMANCE & RELIABILITY

All progression must work reliably.

Persist:
- Current night and progression.
- Unlocked exploration zones.
- Player equipment and proficiency.
- Resources.
- Constructed and upgraded structures.
- Village population and professions.
- Rescued survivors.
- Completed events.
- Boss victories.
- Unlocked blueprints and relics.

Additional requirements:
- Avoid duplicate enemy spawning.
- Avoid broken pathfinding and permanently stuck characters.
- Prevent structures from firing through invalid obstacles.
- Avoid excessive particle and lighting effects that damage performance.
- Clean up defeated enemies and unnecessary effects.
- Ensure UI updates correctly when resources change.
- Ensure world events cannot trigger repeatedly without valid conditions.
- Keep the game stable during large enemy waves.

Use existing save architecture wherever possible. Do not replace a working system unnecessarily.

